		<item>
		<title>The Hip Hop Word Count: Blue Scholars Approved</title>
		<link>http://bluescholars.com/blog/the-hip-hop-word-count-blue-scholars-approved/</link>
		<comments>http://bluescholars.com/blog/the-hip-hop-word-count-blue-scholars-approved/#comments</comments>
		<pubDate>Mon, 31 Jan 2011 17:32:30 +0000</pubDate>
		<dc:creator>Hollis</dc:creator>
				<category><![CDATA[Arts/Culture]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Web]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Blue Scholars]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Hip-hop Word Count]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Tahir Hemphill]]></category>

		<guid isPermaLink="false">http://bluescholars.com/blog/?p=2820</guid>
		<description><![CDATA[<p><a href="http://02cd02a.netsolhost.com/blog/the-hip-hop-word-count-blue-scholars-approved/kmba-rap-lyric-cntr/" rel="attachment wp-att-2914"></a></p>
<p>We wanted to let everyone know about this proposed project, <a href="https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/1801076626/the-hip-hop-word-count-a-searchable-rap-almanac">The Hip Hop Word Count: A Searchable Rap Almanac</a>, that takes being a hip-hop head to brainiac status. This guy <strong>Tahir Hemphill</strong> is the mastermind behind the project,&#8230; <a href="http://bluescholars.com/blog/the-hip-hop-word-count-blue-scholars-approved/" class="read_more">More</a></p>]]></description>
			<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><a href="http://02cd02a.netsolhost.com/blog/the-hip-hop-word-count-blue-scholars-approved/kmba-rap-lyric-cntr/" rel="attachment wp-att-2914"><img src="http://02cd02a.netsolhost.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2011/01/kmba-rap-lyric-cntr-500x260.png" alt="" title="kmba-rap-lyric-cntr" width="500" height="260" class="alignnone size-medium wp-image-2914" /></a></p>
<p>We wanted to let everyone know about this proposed project, <a href="https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/1801076626/the-hip-hop-word-count-a-searchable-rap-almanac">The Hip Hop Word Count: A Searchable Rap Almanac</a>, that takes being a hip-hop head to brainiac status. This guy <strong>Tahir Hemphill</strong> is the mastermind behind the project, which he describes thusly:</p>
<blockquote><p><em>How can analyzing lyrics teach us about our culture?</em></p>
<p><em>The Hip-Hop Word Count locks in a time and geographic location for every metaphor, simile, cultural reference, phrase, meme and socio-political idea used in the corpus of Hip-Hop.</p>
<p>The Hip-Hop Word Count then converts this data into explorable visualisations which help us to comprehend this vast set of cultural data.</p>
<p></em><em>This data can be used to chart the migration of ideas and builds a geography of language and is the engine for a teaching curriculum.</em></p></blockquote>
<p>As students, we learn that cultures are remembered and live on through how they&#8217;re documented, be it oral tradition, historical record, or otherwise. Hip-hop as a culture has its own documentation: its lyricism. Often times, academic takes on hip-hop forgo its own self-expression and context, with a anthropological, subjective and theory-heavy approach that zaps the authenticity out of the account. This is the genius of this project: a top-level, thorough and accessible platform to let rap lyrics&#8211; and hip-hop&#8211; speak for themselves, with infinite possibilities as to how it&#8217;s applied.</p>
<p>As of this writing, the project needs only $2,000 more to become reality. If you got the guap, consider donating to this project. And you might even get a cool, tasty Rap Chocolate out of it.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
			<wfw:commentRss>http://bluescholars.com/blog/the-hip-hop-word-count-blue-scholars-approved/feed/</wfw:commentRss>
		<slash:comments>4</slash:comments>
		</item>
		<item>
		<title>MLK Day (Mon, 1/17) Workshop: End Police Violence, Deportation and Suvelliance Now!</title>
		<link>http://bluescholars.com/blog/mlk-day-mon-117-workshop-end-police-violence-deportation-and-suvelliance-now/</link>
		<comments>http://bluescholars.com/blog/mlk-day-mon-117-workshop-end-police-violence-deportation-and-suvelliance-now/#comments</comments>
		<pubDate>Thu, 13 Jan 2011 23:51:07 +0000</pubDate>
		<dc:creator>Geo</dc:creator>
				<category><![CDATA[Events]]></category>

		<guid isPermaLink="false">http://bluescholars.com/blog/?p=2861</guid>
		<description><![CDATA[<p></p>
<p>Four seconds. That&#8217;s how long it took for SPD Officer Ian Birk to gun down <strong>John T. Williams</strong> in broad daylight last August 30, as evidenced in this dashboard video that was ordered released by a judge last month.&#8230; <a href="http://bluescholars.com/blog/mlk-day-mon-117-workshop-end-police-violence-deportation-and-suvelliance-now/" class="read_more">More</a></p>]]></description>
			<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><object classid="clsid:d27cdb6e-ae6d-11cf-96b8-444553540000" width="480" height="385" codebase="http://download.macromedia.com/pub/shockwave/cabs/flash/swflash.cab#version=6,0,40,0"><param name="allowFullScreen" value="true" /><param name="allowscriptaccess" value="always" /><param name="src" value="http://www.youtube.com/v/vcxqyp2wOzE?fs=1&amp;hl=en_US" /><param name="allowfullscreen" value="true" /><embed type="application/x-shockwave-flash" width="480" height="385" src="http://www.youtube.com/v/vcxqyp2wOzE?fs=1&amp;hl=en_US" allowscriptaccess="always" allowfullscreen="true"></embed></object></p>
<p>Four seconds. That&#8217;s how long it took for SPD Officer Ian Birk to gun down <strong>John T. Williams</strong> in broad daylight last August 30, as evidenced in this dashboard video that was ordered released by a judge last month. This week, <a href="http://seattletimes.nwsource.com/html/localnews/2013914908_inquest13m.html">the inquest into this shooting</a> began at the King County Courthouse. Since I&#8217;ve posted this video on Facebook and Twitter and even <a href="http://abovegroundmagazine.com/news/culture-news/11/19/geologic-blue-scholars-asks-seattle-mayor-to-investigate-alleged-police-misconduct/">put out this open call to the mayor</a>, we&#8217;ve been getting hit up by folks asking how they can take action.</p>
<p>First and foremost: stay posted on all the updates surrounding this case on our local news outlets, particularly independent sources such as <a href="http://slog.thestranger.com/slog/archives/2011/01/11/day-two-wrap-up-officer-ian-birk-testifies-on-williams-shooting">The Stranger</a>. Second, there&#8217;s been a resurgence of community forums and workshops addressing police violence. Next Monday morning on Martin Luther King, Jr. Day, prior to the annual MLK rally and march at noon, several workshops will be held at <strong>Garfield High School</strong>. We encourage folks to hit up <strong><em>End Police Violence, Deportation and Suvelliance Now!</em></strong>, conducted by Lynn Domingo in room 217.</p>
<p>For more info on this workshops and MLK Day events, <a href="http://www.mlkseattle.org/MLKWorkshops_2011.php">go here</a>.<br />
<a href="http://02cd02a.netsolhost.com/blog/mlk-day-mon-117-workshop-end-police-violence-deportation-and-suvelliance-now/tumblr_ldx6vgxw691qaeev7o1_1280/" rel="attachment wp-att-2917"><img src="http://02cd02a.netsolhost.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2011/01/tumblr_ldx6vgxW691qaeev7o1_1280-500x375.jpg" alt="" title="tumblr_ldx6vgxW691qaeev7o1_1280" width="500" height="375" class="alignnone size-medium wp-image-2917" /></a></p>
]]></content:encoded>
			<wfw:commentRss>http://bluescholars.com/blog/mlk-day-mon-117-workshop-end-police-violence-deportation-and-suvelliance-now/feed/</wfw:commentRss>
		<slash:comments>3</slash:comments>
